From e1a4f50d0fe3ffcb62c2807a8a87e9fd278080c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:22:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: batch M4 memory publication and clean only dirty
 pages

Skip unchanged firmware allocations and page tables during cache maintenance. Read-only UAT walks no longer allocate or dirty tracking metadata. Record table edits and new zero tables before publication, retaining ownership across allocation failures.

Batch live writes and queue clearing across pages with two barriers per range, and publish TVB growth entries together before the existing count/reply barriers. Preserve cache invalidation, TLB ordering, and context/device memory lifetimes.

Validated with actual Rust methods under a host page/cache model, including cross-page guards and allocation failures; warning-free kernel build 044; and M4 boot 023 tests covering UAPI, async bursts, pending teardown, mixed/partial rendering, TVB growth/refusal, indirect compute, GPU aliases, compressed ZLS, spilling, and delayed dependencies/timestamps.

(cherry picked from commit f61af905d49ddaebede60ffeb9bd9e76d2b5445c)
